// **The reason the continuation is explicit.** In C and Python two adjacent string literals are
// one string, so a forgotten comma in a vertical list of strings joins two of them and compiles.
// Here it is a syntax error, and this fixture is what keeps it one: it is the case the design
// chose `\` over bare adjacency to protect, and nothing else would notice if that changed.
fn main() {
    val names = [
        "insert",
        "update",
        "find"
        "find_all"
    ]
    print(prelude.len(names))
}
